          "explanation": "The study used wrist-worn accelerometer data from about 25,000 UK Biobank adults who reported no exercise, then followed their health over time. It found an association between around three one-minute vigorous bursts a day and roughly 40% lower mortality. The tempting wrong answer is a randomized trial, but this design cannot prove cause, since healthier people may naturally move more vigorously. The small lab study describes Dunstan 2012 instead.",
