          "explanation": "PACE found median recovery of about 17 days with acetaminophen (regular or as-needed) versus 16 days on placebo -- no meaningful difference in pain, function, or sleep. The tempting answer is that a regular schedule works better, since steady dosing sounds logical, but the regular-dose group did no better either. All groups did receive reassurance and advice to stay active, which likely drove much of the recovery.",
